# Bench mode only (ros2_roamadome enable_bench_mode): one absolute, home-relative
# position move, sent to the firmware as :DPA<target_deg>. The firmware runs the
# move to completion on its own (REACHED TARGET or its position timeout); the host
# cannot cancel it. Repeating the call with the same target and speed refreshes the bench
# heartbeat without re-sending the move; DomeBenchDrive with percent 0 releases
# the bench claim once the dome is at rest. Repeating the call with a different target or
# speed_percent re-sends the move.
uint16 target_deg   # 0..359
uint8 speed_percent # 0 = the firmware's SpeedTarget (or the plugin's position_move_speed_percent), else 1..100, sent as :DPA<deg>,<percent>; the firmware floors it at MinSpeed and restores SpeedTarget when the move ends
---
bool success
string message
